# Env diagnostic: compare auth behavior across local / dev / prd
#
# Setup (Cursor/VS Code REST Client):
# 1. Set firebaseApiKey in requests/http-client.env.json (from .env.dev / FIREBASE_API_KEY)
# 2. Select environment: dev or prd (bottom-right in editor)
# 3. Run "Get anonymous Firebase token" below, copy idToken into http-client.env.json -> token
# 4. Re-select environment and run the comparison requests
#
# Expected when token + env are correct: 200 on protected reads.
# Same token must work on dev AND prd if both use the same Firebase project + service account.

### 0) Baseline — no auth (both envs should return 401, message: No authorization header found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/app-settings

### 0b) Baseline — invalid token (both envs should return 401, message: Authentication failed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/app-settings
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.here

### 1) Get anonymous Firebase token (same flow as Flutter app)
# @name anonymousSignUp
POST https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signUp?key={{firebaseApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "returnSecureToken": true
}

### Copy response idToken into http-client.env.json for the selected environment.

### 2) App settings — primary cold-start read
GET {{baseUrl}}/app-settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3) Bootstrap bundle (exists on dev; prod may return 404 if not deployed yet)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bootstrap
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4) Downtime status
GET {{baseUrl}}/downtime
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5) Backend health (requires auth; nginx /health is separate and needs no token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6) User profile — replace USER_ID with sub/uid from JWT (jwt.io)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/USER_ID/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7) Sign in with password (admin / test user) — alternative token source
# @name passwordSignIn
POST https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:signInWithPassword?key={{firebaseApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "your-password",
  "returnSecureToken": true
}
